{
    "schemaVersion": 1,
    "script": "scripts/audit-scope-containment.mjs",
    "subject": "Two geometric invariants over every fixture example: a child's extent lies inside its parent's, and no two siblings claim the same byte.",
    "purpose": "Fifty-eight rows, five causes, and the sibling half is what earns this oracle. Containment alone cannot see the emphasis defect: ***a** gives a Text spanning columns 1..3 and a Strong starting at column 1, and both sit inside their paragraph, so the only statement that catches it is that two nodes claim one byte. This cannot be an upstream comparison either - cmark-gfm re-parents emphasis the same way and takes a link's start from the closing bracket the same way, so it would return agreement on exactly the rows that are wrong. Nodes with no position are skipped, not judged; the 0:0..0:0 sentinel and line zero are scripts/audit-scope-sanity.mjs's subject, and two ratchets that claim the same row can each be satisfied by it moving to the other. Every row's closedBy names the step that is expected to clear it; the three H14 rows name no step because none exists yet, and that is the honest state rather than a guess.",
